---@class FMinimalViewInfo
---@field public Location FVector @Location
---@field public Rotation FRotator @Rotation
---@field public FOV number @The horizontal field of view (in degrees) in perspective mode (ignored in orthographic mode).
---@field public DesiredFOV number @The originally desired horizontal field of view before any adjustments to account for different aspect ratios
---@field public FirstPersonFOV number @The horizontal field of view (in degrees) used for primitives tagged as "IsFirstPerson".
---@field public FirstPersonScale number @The scale to apply to primitives tagged as "IsFirstPerson". This is used to scale down primitives towards the camera such that they are small enough not to intersect with the scene.
---@field public OrthoWidth number @The desired width (in world units) of the orthographic view (ignored in Perspective mode)
---@field public bAutoCalculateOrthoPlanes boolean @Option for the Ortho camera to automatically calculated the near/far plane
---@field public AutoPlaneShift number @Manually adjusts the planes of this camera, maintaining the distance between them. Positive moves out to the farplane, negative towards the near plane
---@field public bUpdateOrthoPlanes boolean @Adjusts the near/far planes and the view origin of the current camera automatically to avoid clipping and light artefacting
---@field public bUseCameraHeightAsViewTarget boolean @If UpdateOrthoPlanes is enabled, this setting will use the cameras current height to compensate the distance to the general view (as a pseudo distance to view target when one isn't present)
---@field public OrthoNearClipPlane number @The near plane distance of the orthographic view (in world units)
---@field public OrthoFarClipPlane number @The far plane distance of the orthographic view (in world units)
---@field public PerspectiveNearClipPlane number @The near plane distance of the perspective view (in world units). Set to a negative value to use the default global value of GNearClippingPlane
---@field public AspectRatio number @Aspect Ratio (Width/Height)
---@field public bConstrainAspectRatio boolean @If bConstrainAspectRatio is true, black bars will be added if the destination view has a different aspect ratio than this camera requested.
---@field public bUseFirstPersonParameters boolean @If bUseFirstPersonParameters is true, FirstPersonFOV and FirstPersonScale should be applied to primitives tagged as "IsFirstPerson".
---@field public bUseFieldOfViewForLOD boolean @If true, account for the field of view angle when computing which level of detail to use for meshes.
---@field public ProjectionMode integer @The type of camera
---@field public PostProcessBlendWeight number @Indicates if PostProcessSettings should be applied.
---@field public PostProcessSettings FPostProcessSettings @Post-process settings to use if PostProcessBlendWeight is non-zero.
---@field public OffCenterProjectionOffset FVector2D @Off-axis / off-center projection offset as proportion of screen dimensions
---@field public OverscanResolutionFraction number @Resolution fraction that scales with the amount of overscan added to the view
---@field public CropFraction number @The fraction between 0.0 and 1.0 of the view to crop to during the final post process upscale, with 1.0 meaning no crop
---@field public AsymmetricCropFraction FVector4f @Experimental: The fraction for each edge between 0.0 and 1.0 of the view to crop to during the final post process upscale, with 1.0 meaning no crop. By convention, X is the left edge, Y is the right edge, Z is the top edge, and W is the bottom edge. Stacks with uniform CropFraction.
